# KronoLatch Project Standards (.cursorrules)

# Architecture & Philosophy
- KronoLatch is a deterministic-first, offline-first trip orchestrator.
- Deterministic math MUST always precede GenAI synthesis: never guess transit times, leeway buffers, or domain verifications.
- Python packages are managed with `uv` (Python 3.12+).
- Client-side web application in `/web` is zero-build static HTML/CSS/JS deployed to GitHub Pages.

# Python Code Standards
- Strict type hinting with Pydantic v2 models in `src/kronolatch/models.py`.
- Format and lint with `ruff` (100 char line limit).
- All CLI commands implemented with `typer` and formatted with `rich`.
- When modifying DAG math or domain verification, always verify with:
  `uv run pytest` and `uv run kronolatch self-test`.

# Anti-Phishing Domain Rules
- Always normalize URLs to canonical root domains (eTLD+1) before comparison.
- Preserve the 4-status classification: `VERIFIED_OFFICIAL`, `TRUSTED_AGGREGATOR`, `HIGH_RISK_CLONE`, `UNVERIFIED_THIRD_PARTY`.
- Any candidate URL exhibiting >15% price markup or root domain mismatch with deceptive tokens must be flagged as `HIGH_RISK_CLONE` and blocked.

# Temporal DAG Invariants
- Fixed nodes (`type: "fixed"`) cannot shift departure/entry times.
- Transit edges must include transit time + station/security overhead + risk buffer.
- When slack is negative, emit `HARD_CONFLICT` and run `optimize_and_cut` to compress/trim flexible nodes.
